.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "Lilconfig ⚙️"
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP \fR\fP

.PP
A zero-dependency alternative to \fRcosmiconfig\fP with the same API\&.
.SH "Installation"
.PP
.PP
.nf
npm install lilconfig
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
import {lilconfig, lilconfigSync} from 'lilconfig';

// all keys are optional
const options = {
    stopDir: '/Users/you/some/dir',
    searchPlaces: ['package\&.json', 'myapp\&.conf\&.js'],
    ignoreEmptySearchPlaces: false
}

lilconfig(
    'myapp',
    options // optional
)\&.search() // Promise<LilconfigResult>

lilconfigSync(
    'myapp',
    options // optional
)\&.load(pathToConfig) // LilconfigResult

/**
 * LilconfigResult
 * {
 *   config: any; // your config
 *   filepath: string;
 * }
 */
.fi
.PP
.SH "ESM"
.PP
ESM configs can be loaded with \fBasync API only\fP\&. Specifically \fRjs\fP files in projects with \fR"type": "module"\fP in \fRpackage\&.json\fP or \fRmjs\fP files\&.
.SH "Difference to \fRcosmiconfig\fP"
.PP
Lilconfig does not intend to be 100% compatible with \fRcosmiconfig\fP but tries to mimic it where possible\&. The key difference is \fBno\fP support for yaml files out of the box(\fRlilconfig\fP attempts to parse files with no extension as JSON instead of YAML)\&. You can still add the support for YAML files by providing a loader, see an \fBexample\fP below\&.
.SS "Options difference between the two\&."
cosmiconfig option  lilconfig  cache  ✅  loaders  ✅  ignoreEmptySearchPlaces  ✅  packageProp  ✅  searchPlaces  ✅  stopDir  ✅  transform  ✅  
.SH "Loaders examples"
.PP
.SS "Yaml loader"
If you need the YAML support you can provide your own loader

.PP
.PP
.nf
import {lilconfig} from 'lilconfig';
import yaml from 'yaml';

function loadYaml(filepath, content) {
    return yaml\&.parse(content);
}

const options = {
    loaders: {
        '\&.yaml': loadYaml,
        '\&.yml': loadYaml,
        // loader for files with no extension
        noExt: loadYaml
    }
};

lilconfig('myapp', options)
    \&.search()
    \&.then(result => {
        result // {config, filepath}
    });
.fi
.PP
